{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/896277-how-do-pacts-work","id":896277,"title":"How do pacts work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-22T13:43:55-07:00","id":896277,"title":"How do pacts work?","content":"I am preparing a first session of Demon next weekend, and I was reviewing the Pacts section. The first time I read them I loved the idea, and I don't know how but I understood that the demon actually had to do something in the pact. For example, if the mortal wanted to kill his enemy in exchange for a part of her life, the demon was the one in charge of dismissing his enemy.<br /> For what I am reading now in my revision of this chapter, what the mortal asks in the pact is something that happens automatically after signing. The example in the book is a mortal asking for riches, and how they appear &quot;from nowhere&quot;.<br /> <br /> Therefore... Isn't it easier to have a mortal friend wishing for, literally, anything the demon is interested in? Information about the god machine, destruction of architecture or facilities, power for the demon, death for certain angels... The demon only have to take in exchange minor things in her life, or nothing at all.<br /> <br /> The idea of Pacts is nice and interesting, but the section on the book doesn't give a clear mechanic about what can or cannot do a pact automatically, or what has to do the demon for that (apart from spending willpower), or how do they really work...<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11574-andarea","name":"Andarea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:53:27-07:00","id":896287,"title":"","content":"Pacts are kind of a backdoor in reality. The demon rearranges the ledger book of existence and it's easier on the demon if both sides balance out (ignoring unbalanced pacts in favour of the mortal) because at the end of the day the books balance out. That's how I explain the extra willpower cost.<br /> <br /> A demon can give what is listed through the assets and related sections to their respective parties but anything that does not fall in those categories the demon must do themself. For instance to raise a dead loved one a demon may get a pact set up to extort a benifit for themself but they must still bring the loven one back themself, likely through the raise dead exploit .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}